          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भाग्यम् — bhāgyam — \"luck; fortune\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "यदि भाग्यम् अस्ति, तर्हि सर्वं सुखं भविष्यति। yadi bhāgyam asti, tarhi sarvaṃ sukhaṃ bhaviṣyati. If we have luck, all will be well."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भाग्यम् (bhāgyam) comes from the root √bhaj, \"to share\" (MW takes bhāgya as \"to be shared\"), and MW gives the neuter bhāgya \"fate, destiny, fortune, good fortune\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
